      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the physical aspect, but i'm having a hard time picturing how the air \"decides\" to move that way. like, is there a way to think about it using a metaphor or a simple analogy to make it easier to remember for the test? something that explains why the air behaves so predictably?",
